& [Situation]
  + Cantor already compiles admits queries and reflects over proof-bearing SOP artifacts but its single governing behavior remains distributed across subsystem language
  + the user has now named that behavior as speak into order and has related self-assembly to Cantor reading its own governed identity
  + Holographic Attention independently specifies intention grip protected semantic projection intuition capture saturation de-inference and ordered semantic discharge
  + premature composition would either force imagination into authority or let speculative coherence authorize itself

& [Justification]
  + a stable top-level Cantor identity is needed so retrieval attention procedures faculties and self-hosting can be evaluated against one purpose
  + intuition must be captured before articulation but remain non-authoritative until its support and contradictions are reconstructed
  + Security and Honesty admission must precede Observer interpretation so no faculty package validates itself through its own claims
  + prompt schema faculty and tool language must be accounted as active attention stimuli because live Holographic Attention experiments observed competing instruction grip and metric capture
  + external project semantics require exact receipt Cantor-local processing and later cryptographic compilation before executable admission

& [Solution]
  + define SpeakIntoOrderEpisode as a deterministic host-visible protocol from trusted boot and focused intention through protected candidate expansion ordered resolution independent grounding and proof-bearing emission
  + define ProtectedImaginationChamber as a derived sandbox whose candidates can influence inspection but cannot mutate or authorize the admitted fabric
  + define IntuitionCapture as a pre-articulation candidate record followed by a separately recorded ArticulationPass
  + define DirectiveGripAccount so every loaded control phrase schema and tool declaration remains observable input rather than invisible control state
  + define SelfAssembly as dependency planning and candidate compilation from Cantor's admitted identity while preserving an externally pinned bootstrap and explicit authorization gate
  + stage implementation after the current lexical sidecar and query dependencies rather than bypassing their active locks

& [Delineation]
  + speak into order is not eloquent response generation
  + protected imagination is not admitted knowledge
  + intuition capture is not proof or hidden-state access
  + semantic satisfaction signatures are not cryptographic recognition certificates
  + self-assembly is not self-authorization self-originating trust or autonomous effects
  + Honesty evaluates representation coherence and source fidelity while Security evaluates authority boundary and permitted transition; neither establishes universal truth or safety

& [DataDrivenDesign]
  + primary identities are boot manifest trust receipt attention episode focused intention observation candidate intuition articulation directive grip semantic line grounding ledger and emission
  + authoritative admitted derived candidate and emitted states remain distinct
  + every transform binds source generation configuration budget and digest
  + unresolved ambiguity contradiction non-fire and budget stop are valid terminal outcomes

& [SevenFoldTrace]
  + [fold_1] preserves raw user dictation and exact cross-project artifact receipts
  + [fold_2] separates bootstrap admission observation protected projection resolution grounding emission and effects
  + [fold_3] models identities transitions gates budgets evidence provenance and rollback
  + [fold_4] projects divergent candidate meanings without changing source authority
  + [fold_5] converges through purpose fitness hard boundaries de-inference ordered-line completeness and independent grounding
  + [fold_6] attacks circular trust narrative intoxication prompt grip self-confirmation stale import partial line firing and self-authorization
  + [fold_7] phase-locks conceptual identity and dependency order while retaining separate implementation activation

& [Disposition]
  + [status] canonical_formation_justified
  + [implementation_authority] absent_pending_slice_activation
  + [model_routing] architecture and cross-system integration require deeper reasoning; later bounded Rust forms tests fixtures and ledger updates are Spark-suitable
